WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:08.150
Gold Roger, the legendary King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

3
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.890
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

4
00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:17.430
You want my treasure? Go ahead. Find it!

5
00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.830
Everything is right where I left it!

6
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.840
Pirates have set out in pursuit of their dreams!

7
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:25.440
The world has truly entered... the Great Pirate Era!

8
00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:29.380
Gotta keep movin’, just can't stop

9
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.780
Rarin’ for the dawn to arrive

10
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.480
One, two, sunshine, four, we go!

11
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:43.290
Hoist the flag for the break of romance dawn

12
00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:49.500
Jump-start your day, ready to make waves

13
00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.200
Reachin’ for fantastic realms

14
00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.370
Need to put your toughness on display

15
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.680
Is bein’ brazen such a crime?

16
00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.480
If you’re wanted, you’re a winner

17
00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:09.620
Ah, freedom is our only rule

18
00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:15.660
Worries don’t bother us at all

19
00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.430
Keep on goin’, that's our pledge

20
00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:22.030
Since the day our dreams began

21
00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:26.870
Our aims remain the same

22
00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:29.240
Sunlight won’t fade from our hearts

23
00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.670
The sun of my heart will never set

24
00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:40.450
One, two, sunshine... One, two, sunshine

25
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:47.850
One, two, sunshine, four, we go!

26
00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:51.930
We go!

27
00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:58.570
What did you say, Luffy?!

28
00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:01.670
Let's tame the octopus
and make him pull our ship!

29
00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:03.870
<b>Adventure in the Deep Sea</b>

30
00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:03.140
No way!

31
00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:08.810
Take a good look! No, you don't have
to take a good look since it's huge!

32
00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:11.280
Oh, it's big!

33
00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.720
We're dead!

34
00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.790
It must've been around
for several hundred years!

35
00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:19.020
The kraken appears
in many myths in the world!

36
00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:22.290
It's like a visionary creature!

37
00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.800
It has no bones...

38
00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:27.030
and I'm a skeleton without any flesh...

39
00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:31.000
It's the polar opposite of me.

40
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.340
I don't care!

41
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.610
You're quite good.

42
00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.110
You can't see this kind of thing often, so...

43
00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:39.840
Sketching? How relaxed?!

44
00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.680
I'll help you, but do you have a plan, Luffy?

45
00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.620
The problem is that we're in the sea.

46
00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:49.290
No. No. No.

47
00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:52.760
The problem is the size of it.

48
00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.990
It would be dangerous
even if we were on land.

49
00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:58.460
What's wrong with them?

50
00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:04.470
This is the kind of situation when everybody
agrees to run away at full speed!

51
00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:06.700
Shift the helm to the south!

52
00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.640
Hey, Nami, go straight towards the octopus!

53
00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.140
Don't be a fool!
Listen to me!

54
00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.940
The octopus will...
Whoa, whoa, Nami.

55
00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:14.550
I'm here for...

56
00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.550
here for...

57
00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:21.390
for you!

58
00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:22.950
You held it!

59
00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.090
Good job!

60
00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:27.620
Thanks to the rehabilitation
and to Nami for wearing a coat.

61
00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:31.600
It's dangerous to be on this ship!
I've got to protect myself!

62
00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:33.860
Something's coming from behind!

63
00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:38.800
Brother!

64
00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:39.740
They came back!

65
00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.240
Coribou! Guys!

66
00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.010
We're gonna save my brother!

67
00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.210
– Yes!
– Yes!

68
00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:51.420
You came back to save me, huh?!

69
00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:58.460
Don't do it!

70
00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:03.990
The coating popped!

71
00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:06.560
That ship is even bigger than the Sunny!

72
00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.740
Guys!

73
00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:21.710
They look like jellyfish.

74
00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:24.180
Shut up, Roronoa! Cut it out!

75
00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:27.420
It's coming!

76
00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:32.020
It's too big!

77
00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:34.690
How can we fight against it?!

78
00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:36.030
Gear Thir–

79
00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:38.530
No!

80
00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:40.660
You'll break the bubble!

81
00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:45.670
Chicken Voyage!

82
00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.770
Can we... get away somehow?!

83
00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:52.040
Don't do anything! I'll beat it!

84
00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:55.310
No! You're gonna break the bubble!

85
00:04:55.650 --> 00:05:01.490
Listen! If you wanna fight
against it that much, here is an idea!

86
00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:02.050
Huh?

87
00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:04.350
What is it? Tell me.

88
00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:07.820
Okay, that's good!

89
00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:11.330
That's the extra-vehicular flutter kick coating!

90
00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.030
An extra-vehicular diving suit!

91
00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:20.840
As long as you're in it,
you can even fight in water!

92
00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:25.110
If I let these fools do whatever
they want, I'll be in danger too!

93
00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:27.410
You shouldn't have done that, stranger!

94
00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.980
We wanted to run away!

95
00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:32.080
Now, they're gonna fight!

96
00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:38.020
I told you guys to run from the beginning
but that captain won't listen!

97
00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:42.660
Would you rather they fought on this ship?

98
00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:44.660
Okay, good luck!

99
00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:45.730
Go far away!

100
00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:47.230
This rope is annoying.

101
00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:49.870
Stay away from this ship!

102
00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.030
Alright.

103
00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:53.200
Okay, let's go!

104
00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:54.040
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

105
00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:56.770
Huh?

106
00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:58.480
Wait!

107
00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:00.340
You have to attach the safety rope!

108
00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:02.910
You'll be separated!

109
00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:05.380
Nami's worrying about me!

110
00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:07.050
You guys!

111
00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.720
Draw his attention for me!

112
00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:11.960
I'm gonna beat him with one strong blow!

113
00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:15.230
I could beat him right away!

114
00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:17.190
You can't cut him!

115
00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:19.800
I want the octopus as a pet!

116
00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:23.330
Are they okay?

117
00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:26.240
Stay as far away as you can!
Even a millimeter...

118
00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:30.040
But it's attacking us!

119
00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:31.810
Move aside, guys!

120
00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:35.450
Franky...

121
00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:41.020
Rocket Launcher!

122
00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:43.990
It deflected the tentacle!

123
00:06:43.990 --> 00:06:45.890
How powerful!

124
00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:49.230
No, another arm!

125
00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:50.860
Why does it keep coming after us?!

126
00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:54.100
Guard Point!

127
00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:57.100
They got hit hard!

128
00:06:58.240 --> 00:06:59.800
Are you guys okay?

129
00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:03.540
Th-That was close!

130
00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:04.640
Well done!

131
00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:06.110
Yeah, Chopper!

132
00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:11.320
We're gonna hit a sea mount!

133
00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:13.820
Mil Fleurs!

134
00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:16.020
Gigantesco Mano!

135
00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:22.830
What big hands!

136
00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:25.830
– Yes!
– Yes!

137
00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:28.670
That's our Robin! We're saved!

138
00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:31.440
Good.

139
00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:35.240
Although I'm in water, I was okay
because it was just a brief moment.

140
00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:38.910
Alright, it's my turn!

141
00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:43.780
Gear Third!

142
00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.870
Armament: Hardening!

143
00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:12.940
The sea is sapping my strength!

144
00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:18.680
That damn octopus! Is it trying to stop him?

145
00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:20.650
Blue Walk!

146
00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:24.450
What? Sanji left his bubble!

147
00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:26.690
Never mind that! Look at that speed!

148
00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:28.130
He's like a fishman!

149
00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:29.030
Cool!

150
00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:31.460
I ran and ran...

151
00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:34.300
from those abominations for two years.

152
00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:38.400
Compared to them, this monster is nothing.

153
00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:40.040
I'd even say it's cute.

154
00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.240
Diable Jambe!

155
00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:48.980
Bien Cuit...

156
00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:51.520
Grill Shot!

157
00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.730
Three-Sword Style Secret Technique...

158
00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:04.260
Crossing the Six Paths!

159
00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:16.940
Hey, hey, Zoro! Sanji!

160
00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:19.440
You can't cut his arms!

161
00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:21.750
Gum-Gum...

162
00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:27.150
Elephant Gun!

163
00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:34.360
He knocked it out!

164
00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:37.160
He's gotten so much stronger!

165
00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:44.940
Huh? Something's in there!

166
00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:45.870
– What?
– Huh?

167
00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:48.170
A shark?

168
00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:54.850
A shark?

169
00:09:54.850 --> 00:09:57.110
Isn't that shark wearing something?

170
00:09:57.110 --> 00:09:59.250
It's pretty big.

171
00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:14.660
They've been swept away
by the downward current!

172
00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:17.200
Oh no! Follow them!
We have to stay together!

173
00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:18.500
Okay!

174
00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:24.410
I don't wanna die here!

175
00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:26.040
You've got to be kidding me!

176
00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:27.040
You're still here?

177
00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:27.980
You're too calm!

178
00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:31.010
My eyes are spinning!

179
00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:32.620
But I don't have eyes!

180
00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:38.820
Keep the yard level!

181
00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:42.260
Hard to port! We're gonna crash
into the continental shelf!

182
00:10:43.090 --> 00:10:44.260
I got it!

183
00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:47.030
Keep your focus or the ship will wreck!

184
00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:48.000
What?!

185
00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:51.700
Don't get thrown off!

186
00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:55.510
Stay in the center of the current!

187
00:10:55.970 --> 00:10:57.040
Alright!

188
00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:03.380
It's really fast!

189
00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:06.520
This is fun!

190
00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:19.560
Usopp!

191
00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.370
Oh, ow, ow, ow!

192
00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:25.770
I'm alive!

193
00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:32.540
What? Why are you all so glum?

194
00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:36.280
Oh I know! You guys can't
do anything without me...

195
00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:39.980
It's so cold here!

196
00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:42.720
We can't find Luffy and the other two.

197
00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:43.920
We got separated.

198
00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:45.520
What?!

199
00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:49.230
I hope they haven't been shredded
to pieces by the monster.

200
00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:51.130
Your imagination is terrifying...

201
00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:55.470
It's too dark. I wanna look
for them but I can't see anything!

202
00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:58.200
I'm not good with darkness.

203
00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:01.200
I-I feel something, don't you?

204
00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:04.210
We probably submerged around 7,000 meters.

205
00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:08.180
Even the Shark Submerge
can't take the pressure this deep.

206
00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:10.680
Are we near Fishman Island?

207
00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:13.450
Maybe they got there already...

208
00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:17.820
Camie said it's located
at 10,000 meters below sea level.

209
00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:21.560
We have to submerge 3,000 meters more?!

210
00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:24.490
All they have is a small bubble.

211
00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:27.400
Even if they're alive,
there isn't enough air so it's dangerous!

212
00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:30.800
That's why I told them
to attach the safety rope!

213
00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:33.240
We won't get anything done standing around.

214
00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:34.270
Let's look for them.

215
00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.110
I now have a search light.

216
00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:37.510
– What?!
– What?!

217
00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:40.540
Is it your eyes?!

218
00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:42.710
Franky...

219
00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:47.520
Nipple Lights!

220
00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:49.490
Why there?!

221
00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:55.830
Let's get away!

222
00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:04.300
Luffy!

223
00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:05.900
Zoro!

224
00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:07.670
Sanji!

225
00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:10.240
Where did you go?

226
00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:12.210
Come back!

227
00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:17.580
In this vast, submerged expanse,
the Sunny Eyes don't help that much.

228
00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:20.220
We're stuck...

229
00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:24.050
The darkness is stirring up our anxiety.

230
00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:26.590
In fact, we're not getting anywhere.

231
00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:29.160
What should we do?

232
00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:33.600
We can't stop the ship
so try not to overlook anything.

233
00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:38.900
Oh, it's a jellyfish!

234
00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:40.870
There's a massive jellyfish above us!

235
00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:42.470
That's huge!

236
00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:44.070
You're right!

237
00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:46.640
They're twinkling!

238
00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:49.350
Like stars in the night!

239
00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:51.450
That's beautiful!

240
00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:54.280
Oh, a tentacle!

241
00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:57.050
D-Do you wanna be my friend?

242
00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:59.190
Don't touch it, Chopper!

243
00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:00.390
It's probably venomous!

244
00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:07.330
Oh no!

245
00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:10.700
Mini Coup de Burst!

246
00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:15.640
– Wh-What?!
– Wh-What?!

247
00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:17.770
The jellyfish got eaten!

248
00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:21.610
Oh, we lost some air.

249
00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:23.510
Better than getting eaten!

250
00:14:23.510 --> 00:14:24.050
– Huh?!
– Huh?!

251
00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:28.380
Coup de Burst is a weapon
that shoots a fair amount of air.

252
00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:33.260
But since we're in the water,
we only have a limited amount of air.

253
00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:36.860
So when we shoot the air out,
the bubble shrinks!

254
00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:43.170
The fish that bit it turned upside down!

255
00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:45.170
So they are venomous.

256
00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:46.040
– What?!
– What?!

257
00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:48.770
The deep sea's scary! It's dark too...

258
00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:51.610
There are a lot of fish with white eyes...

259
00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:54.440
It's creepy here!

260
00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:00.920
Since the deep sea is always dark,

261
00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:04.350
there are many creatures
with rudimentary eyes.

262
00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:08.190
So they can't see well.

263
00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:11.160
Fools!

264
00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:12.760
See this? Come here!

265
00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:15.970
But there are some with developed eyes too.

266
00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:22.810
What's that? How can I
see things without eyes?

267
00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:26.480
Do you all want to know the reason?

268
00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:28.750
The answer is...

269
00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:33.480
a secret!

270
00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:37.190
Are you talking to yourself?

271
00:15:37.190 --> 00:15:38.560
No problem.

272
00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:41.060
I'm used to being lonely.

273
00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:43.790
Hey! Stop fooling around and look for them!

274
00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:48.300
Why did I get hit?

275
00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:52.040
– Luffy! Zoro! Sanji!
– Luffy! Zoro! Sanji!

276
00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:54.770
– Where are you?!
– Where are you?!

277
00:15:55.710 --> 00:15:56.940
Oh?

278
00:15:57.770 --> 00:15:59.380
This rope must be...

279
00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.210
Everyone.

280
00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:02.380
Huh?

281
00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:05.750
Have you seen that pirate guy?

282
00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:08.080
Oh yeah, he's still here!

283
00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:10.050
I totally forgot about him.

284
00:16:10.050 --> 00:16:11.550
Where did he go?

285
00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:14.720
I haven't seen him since we got this deep.

286
00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:17.930
Maybe he got thrown off
during the downward pull.

287
00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:19.100
That could be it!

288
00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:24.030
His hands and legs were tied up
so he couldn't hold on to anything.

289
00:16:24.030 --> 00:16:25.240
Well but...

290
00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:26.340
– What?
– What?

291
00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:28.970
He untied himself. See?

292
00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:34.040
Th-Then, he's somewhere on the ship?!

293
00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:36.410
Where is he?

294
00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:38.980
He's got to be hiding somewhere...

295
00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:40.450
What?!

296
00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:42.450
Oh no...

297
00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:48.160
I'll sneak into the girls' room...
if that's what you want, honey.

298
00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:49.860
Damn!

299
00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:53.630
We have enough problems already,
but now we have to look out for him too.

300
00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.230
Who cares?!

301
00:16:55.230 --> 00:16:57.300
He's not that strong anyway.

302
00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:02.010
It's great.

303
00:17:02.970 --> 00:17:09.950
Those formidable three who were fighting
against the kraken went missing.

304
00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:14.220
There's no way they could have
survived after getting lost

305
00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:17.120
with just those bubbles to protect them.

306
00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:21.460
It's a shame that I couldn't kill Straw Hat...

307
00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:31.130
but I can prove that he's dead by killing
these crew members and taking their heads.

308
00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:36.570
But don't rush, Caribou!

309
00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:38.310
You can't rush!

310
00:17:38.310 --> 00:17:42.350
If I kill them here, there's
no one else to sail the ship.

311
00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:45.850
They navigate the ship pretty well.

312
00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:49.420
As soon as you get to Fishman Island...

313
00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:53.290
you all will be dead!

314
00:17:57.960 --> 00:17:59.630
Here he is!

315
00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:03.430
Oh no!

316
00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:08.170
Shoot! Dammit!

317
00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:06.170
Now he can't get away.

318
00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:08.170
How did he get in there?

319
00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:10.370
We weren't paying attention.

320
00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:13.080
If he wasn't so stupid,
we could be in danger now.

321
00:18:13.510 --> 00:18:16.850
His body wasn't taking form.
It melted like mud.

322
00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:18.820
Like mud?

323
00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:21.650
Yeah, I'm sure it's a devil fruit power.

324
00:18:21.650 --> 00:18:24.050
He must've eaten a logia-type fruit.

325
00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:28.660
He was only pretending to be caught.

326
00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:30.160
Hey!

327
00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:33.630
Get me out of here, mister!
Mister in swimshorts!

328
00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:36.300
I'll become your servant!

329
00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:41.600
Huh? What's the matter, Chopper?

330
00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:42.970
I don't know.

331
00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:45.240
I feel hot all of the sudden.

332
00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:47.880
I can't stand the heat.

333
00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:49.810
It's hot!

334
00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:50.910
What happened?

335
00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:53.880
Wh-What's this?

336
00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:55.020
Smoke?

337
00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:56.850
It's blocking our view forward!

338
00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:01.020
Smoke from the sea floor? Why?

339
00:19:01.460 --> 00:19:02.590
It's...

340
00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:04.230
It could be...

341
00:19:10.570 --> 00:19:12.440
Hydrothermal deposits!

342
00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:15.570
A volcanic area in the sea!

343
00:19:15.570 --> 00:19:16.270
What?!

344
00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:18.980
Look, evidence of volcanic eruptions!

345
00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:21.540
Let's get away from here!

346
00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:24.250
If it erupts, we're gonna die!

347
00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:27.480
It's hot... It's hot...!

348
00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:32.290
Something's after us!

349
00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:34.090
Carnivorous tube worms!

350
00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:35.890
We have no choice.

351
00:19:35.890 --> 00:19:38.360
Mini Coup de Burst!

352
00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:44.330
Faceless crabs!

353
00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:46.570
Mini Coup de Burst!

354
00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:50.110
I don't even know what they are!

355
00:19:50.110 --> 00:19:53.140
Mini Coup de Burst!

356
00:19:53.140 --> 00:19:55.280
The deep sea's scary!

357
00:19:56.180 --> 00:20:00.220
Luffy and the others can't survive here.

358
00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:02.050
I'm starting to get sad.

359
00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:04.150
I finally got to see him after two years...

360
00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:07.120
Cut it out! They're not gonna die so easily!

361
00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:12.700
I used Coup de Burst little by little,
but we lost so much air.

362
00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:17.730
What is that?!

363
00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:19.240
It's so bright!

364
00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:22.470
Is that Fishman Island?

365
00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:24.710
Do you think Luffy and the others are there?

366
00:20:24.710 --> 00:20:27.410
We haven't submerged
another 3,000 meters yet.

367
00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:30.480
Who are you?

368
00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:31.410
Hey!

369
00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:33.920
What are you sending
the flashing signals with?!

370
00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:35.520
Do you see anything?

371
00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:37.950
No, it's still too bright.

372
00:20:41.060 --> 00:20:42.490
Oh no!

373
00:20:45.230 --> 00:20:48.030
It's an angler! He tricked us!

374
00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:51.130
We were fooled by the deep-sea hunter!

375
00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:56.440
That was close!

376
00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:58.880
We're totally trapped!

377
00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:00.680
Can we get away...?

378
00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:08.550
What is it this time?!

379
00:21:08.550 --> 00:21:09.990
I-Is it a human?

380
00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:11.920
What the hell is it?!

381
00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:16.190
A monster in the sea that looks like a man...

382
00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:21.100
It's a sea bonze!

383
00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:27.540
He's gonna capsize the ship!

384
00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:31.540
That?!

385
00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:34.140
Hey, Ankoro!

386
00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:35.810
You can't do that!

387
00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:38.680
Don't eat ships!

388
00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:41.280
How many times do I have to tell you?

389
00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:45.590
Captain Vander Decken won't like this!

390
00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:48.390
D-Did he help us?

391
00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:51.660
Let's go! We have to get away anyway!

392
00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:53.460
He is a monster too!

393
00:21:59.800 --> 00:22:05.170
Dead men tell no tales, and they have no desire...

394
00:22:02.810 --> 00:22:04.140
Is that...

395
00:22:04.910 --> 00:22:05.940
me?

396
00:22:05.170 --> 00:22:10.680
in the dark land where even crows can't fly.

397
00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:16.190
Dead men don't need jewels on their finger.

398
00:22:16.190 --> 00:22:21.920
You can't even see somebody's sorrow in the dark.

399
00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:25.930
Look for it!

400
00:22:25.930 --> 00:22:30.400
Sunken treasures are mine!

401
00:22:30.400 --> 00:22:33.870
I am the richest person in the world...

402
00:22:33.870 --> 00:22:38.540
Captain Vander Decken!

403
00:22:42.610 --> 00:22:43.350
Don't tell me it's...!

404
00:22:47.050 --> 00:22:48.150
Even in the sea?!

405
00:22:55.590 --> 00:22:57.430
A ghost ship?!

406
00:22:57.430 --> 00:22:59.800
You shouldn't be so scared!

407
00:23:00.460 --> 00:23:02.470
I turned! For no reason!

408
00:23:03.330 --> 00:23:06.400
Back then, we really thought
you were a ghost!

409
00:23:06.400 --> 00:23:08.700
Th-That's a real one, though!

410
00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:10.340
Look at that sail!

411
00:23:11.170 --> 00:23:14.510
The infamous Flying Dutchman!

412
00:23:14.510 --> 00:23:17.880
It shouldn't exist in the real world!

413
00:23:17.880 --> 00:23:21.750
It happened several hundred years ago.

414
00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:25.150
One stormy day...

415
00:23:25.760 --> 00:23:28.920
the captain of the pirate ship
suddenly lost his mind

416
00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:34.160
and killed his entire crew by throwing them
into the turbulent water, one after another.

417
00:23:34.160 --> 00:23:36.870
And he even cursed the gods!

418
00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:40.270
The name of the captain was Vander Decken...

419
00:23:40.270 --> 00:23:42.540
and the ship was the Flying Dutchman!

420
00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:45.470
The gods got mad at him...

421
00:23:45.470 --> 00:23:52.480
and set him adrift forever
under constant torture!

422
00:23:52.480 --> 00:23:59.490
And the ship right in front of us
is Captain Vander Decken's haunted ship!

423
00:24:00.290 --> 00:24:02.730
Ankoro! Wadatsumi!

424
00:24:02.730 --> 00:24:05.530
We can't seize their treasure
if you eat the ship...

425
00:24:05.530 --> 00:24:07.600
so knock it down!

426
00:24:09.100 --> 00:24:10.670
I got it!

427
00:24:11.730 --> 00:24:13.340
The sea bonze is...

428
00:24:13.340 --> 00:24:15.570
He's our enemy after all!

429
00:24:15.570 --> 00:24:16.570
Franky!

430
00:24:16.570 --> 00:24:17.910
Use Coup de Burst!

431
00:24:17.910 --> 00:24:20.610
I can't! The fuel has run out!

432
00:24:20.610 --> 00:24:23.710
I have to fill up with cola in the energy room!

433
00:24:27.420 --> 00:24:28.450
We don't have time!

434
00:24:29.350 --> 00:24:30.750
No!

435
00:24:30.750 --> 00:24:31.950
He's gonna get us!

436
00:24:45.630 --> 00:24:47.240
Kraken!

437
00:24:52.380 --> 00:24:55.080
The Monster of the Arctic, Kraken?

438
00:25:05.220 --> 00:25:08.260
Alright, that's enough. Stop!

439
00:25:14.900 --> 00:25:15.730
Good job!

440
00:25:18.070 --> 00:25:20.540
Hey!

441
00:25:20.970 --> 00:25:23.840
Luffy! Zoro! Sanji!

442
00:25:23.840 --> 00:25:26.610
I'm glad that you're all alive!

443
00:25:26.610 --> 00:25:28.510
What were you doing?!

444
00:25:28.510 --> 00:25:32.350
Nami my sweet! Robin my love!

445
00:25:32.350 --> 00:25:33.980
We've been looking for you guys!

446
00:25:35.790 --> 00:25:37.790
They're so high-maintenance.

447
00:25:38.350 --> 00:25:39.920
They got lost!

448
00:25:40.360 --> 00:25:41.660
Hey!

449
00:25:41.660 --> 00:25:43.630
Wake up, Wadatsumi!

450
00:25:43.630 --> 00:25:46.600
Avenge yourself! Get back at it!

451
00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:54.700
Well, Sanji's bubble and mine popped,
so we got into Zoro's.

452
00:25:55.910 --> 00:25:57.410
I thought I was gonna die!

453
00:25:57.410 --> 00:25:59.440
Don't make us worry!

454
00:25:59.440 --> 00:26:01.840
Alright, here's a song to celebrate your return.

455
00:26:03.110 --> 00:26:06.020
Lots of space! There's no place like home!

456
00:26:06.020 --> 00:26:08.750
Luffy! I was scared!

457
00:26:10.420 --> 00:26:13.190
You all have an amazing ability to survive.

458
00:26:13.190 --> 00:26:14.690
I can't believe it!

459
00:26:14.690 --> 00:26:18.860
You really tamed the monster octopus?

460
00:26:19.430 --> 00:26:21.930
And are you gonna use the kraken?

461
00:26:21.930 --> 00:26:26.670
Yeah, I'm gonna use him
like experienced people do!

462
00:26:26.670 --> 00:26:27.670
Right, Surume?

463
00:26:27.670 --> 00:26:30.010
That's a squid snack!

464
00:26:30.410 --> 00:26:32.410
Surume!

465
00:26:32.410 --> 00:26:37.710
The kraken is an octopus,
but he named it Surume, oh yeah!

466
00:26:37.710 --> 00:26:40.950
Alright, pull the Sunny, Surume!

467
00:26:41.520 --> 00:26:44.590
Well, instead of making pull the ship,

468
00:26:45.050 --> 00:26:48.090
we have to make sure
that he's not gonna smash it up.

469
00:26:48.090 --> 00:26:50.360
Captain, the pirate ship is...

470
00:26:50.360 --> 00:26:53.200
Don't let it get away! Go after it!

471
00:26:53.200 --> 00:26:55.100
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

472
00:26:59.400 --> 00:27:00.240
What is it?

473
00:27:06.010 --> 00:27:10.050
This is no good, Captain Vander Decken!

474
00:27:13.220 --> 00:27:14.220
Oh no!

475
00:27:14.220 --> 00:27:16.690
The undersea volcano's gonna erupt!

476
00:27:17.290 --> 00:27:19.590
– What?!
– What?!
